# Cline rules for blenderized-tubefeed-calculator

1. Read CONTEXT.md §9 (Current status) FIRST. Trust its checkboxes —
   do not re-do or re-verify completed phases.

2. The backend (data_loader, models, nutrients, calculator, intake,
   measures, targets, report) is COMPLETE and VERIFIED as of 2026-07-19
   (Intake Record rework — see CONTEXT.md §9). Do not rewrite,
   re-scaffold, or re-test these modules unless the user explicitly
   asks or a change breaks them. Reference data (nutrient registry,
   targets, formulas, thinning liquids) lives under data/packs/canada/,
   not data/targets/ or data/formulas/ — those directories no longer
   exist.

   **The single most important invariant to protect: there is
   deliberately NO "over-draw" / batch-mismatch flag anywhere in this
   app.** Daily totals are a direct sum over Intake Record rows
   (`src/intake.py::aggregate_intake()`) — never a schedule volume
   extrapolated against a blend's measured batch volume. That
   extrapolation was a real bug, fixed 2026-07-19; re-adding any
   "logged more than the batch made" check reintroduces it. Read
   `FEED_LOG_REWORK.md` §6.2 before touching `src/intake.py` or the
   Intake Record UI in `app/streamlit_app.py`.

2b. HARD RULES for any feature that calls a paid API (e.g. the
   label-photo extraction planned for Week 4). Agreed 2026-07-30
   BEFORE the feature exists, so it is not renegotiated later:

   **(a) The spend cap ships in the SAME COMMIT as the API call.**
   Not a follow-up task, not a TODO. The app is public at
   https://btfcalc.streamlit.app with the key in Streamlit secrets,
   so every call any visitor makes bills the author personally.
   All three are required: a per-session call limit in
   st.session_state; a spend limit on the key itself in the provider
   console (this is the one that holds when the app code is wrong);
   and a visible per-use notice. Missing any one = the feature does
   not ship. Implementing the call and leaving the cap for later is
   an incomplete task, not a partial success.

   **(b) A photo fills the NFt form; it never writes straight into a
   blend.** Extraction output lands in the existing "custom food from
   label" fields as editable drafts for the RD to read and confirm. A
   misread sodium digit flows into a patient's daily total. The AI is
   a typing shortcut, not a data source, and the UI must say so.

   See CONTEXT.md §11 ("HARD RULES for paid-API features").

3. To verify the backend, run:

   .venv/bin/python scripts/verify_backend.py

   It exits 0 and prints "=== ALL BACKEND MODULES VERIFIED ===" on
   success. If you add backend features, extend that script instead of
   writing a new one-off verification command. For UI changes, build
   a Streamlit AppTest script (see recent commits for the pattern) —
   "imports OK" alone does not prove a UI change works.

4. Current work (2026-07-30): Week 2 is COMPLETE and the app is live
   at https://btfcalc.streamlit.app. Week 3 ("Build to Last") is in
   progress: pytest suite, GitHub Actions CI, runtime/dev dependency
   split, the failing scripts/check_tab_restructure.py, formula-row
   nutrient_coverage, thinning_liquids pack-awareness, and the USDA
   SR Legacy supplement. The Streamlit Cloud deploy sub-item is
   already DONE. The AI-assist features (label-photo extraction,
   PDF → formulas) were moved to Week 4. See CONTEXT.md §9 for the
   sub-item checklist, §1 for the app flow, FEED_LOG_REWORK.md for
   the Intake Record design rationale, and HANDOFF.md for a
   paste-ready prompt.

   **THE UI IS PINNED** (author's instruction, 2026-07-30). She is
   satisfied with the current layout and will revise it herself as
   features land. Do not restructure tabs, retheme, resize type, or
   reorder sections, and do not start the three parked UI items
   (volume-needed planning aid, two-section chart note, Excel export
   review) unasked. See CONTEXT.md §9's pinned-issues list.

5. Never modify anything under cnf_fcen_all-files-data_2026/ (raw data).

6. After completing meaningful work, update CONTEXT.md §9 status and
   commit, so the next session starts from accurate state.
